path: Heavy > grieving    tags: grief
What's happened?  My grandad died last month
Why do you think you feel grieving?  I never got to say goodbye
searched for: My grandfather died last month, and I feel heavy with grief because I never got to say goodbye. I am afraid of what that silence means, and I have not told anyone how much it hurts.

  Helen Keller, The Story of My Life With her letters (1887-1901) and a supplementary account of her education, including passages from the reports and letters of her teacher, Anne Mansfield Sullivan, by John Albert Macy (1880–1968)    match 0.84
  https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2397

    But, however this may be, I cannot now write the letter which has
    lain in my thought for you so long. My heart is too full of sadness
    to dwell upon the happiness the summer has brought me.
  > My father is dead. He died last Saturday at my home in Tuscumbia,
  > and I was not there.
    My own dear loving father! Oh, dear friend, how shall I ever bear
    it!...

  judge: emotion yes, situation yes, cause yes, fear partly; coping: struggling. Her beloved father died while she was not there, and she pours out her grief to a friend, asking how she will ever bear it.

